      "side": 1,
      "message": "`desktop-google` is having automerger from `kernel/common`. That is, all changes landing in the latter, end up in the former. So there should be no compilation issues \n\nIf we have only a one-way dependency, that is, second patch depends on first one, we can merge first on `kernel/common`, and then add the second on `desktop-google`.We unfortunately cannot ensure atomic submit (like topic) across two gerrit hosts.",
